[267.600681, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m6\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[267.610503, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe visual system and interactive behaviors are in place. Next I’ll generate the semantic HTML for the three required pages and individual blog posts, using the\r\nCV details as the content source.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/my_website && cat > scripts/generate_site.py <<'PY'\r\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Generate the static research-profile site from a small content model.\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nfrom html import escape\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\r\n\r\nNAME = \"Lydia Moreno\"\r\nEMAIL = \"lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu\"\r\nGITHUB = \"https://github.com/lydia-moreno\"\r\nTWITTER = \"https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab\"\r\n\r\nRESEARCH_INTERESTS = [\r\n    (\r\n        \"Neural Encoding & Decoding\",\r\n        \"Developing interpretable models that translate spike-train data into behavioral predictions.\",\r\n        '<path d=\"M4 12h3l2.2-6 3.1 12L15 9l1.7 3H20\"/>',\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"Machine Learning for Biomedical Imaging\",\r\n        \"Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to magnetic resonance and two-photon microscopy data.\",\r\n        '<rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M8 5v14M16 5v14M3 12h18\"/>',\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"Single-Cell Omics\",\r\n        \"Designing scalable pipelines for integrating multi-modal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.\",\r\n        '<circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"8\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle cx=\"16.5\" cy=\"6.5\" r=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"16\" r=\"2.4\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"16.5\" r=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M9 9.5 \r\n11 14M15 8l-2 6\"/>',\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"Explainable AI in Neuroscience\",\r\n        \"Building frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in black-box models.\",\r\n        '<path d=\"M12 3v3M12 18v3M3 12h3M18 12h3M5.6 5.6l2.1 2.1M16.3 16.3l2.1 2.1M18.4 5.6l-2.1 2.1M7.7 16.3l-2.1 2.1\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3.5\"/>',\r\n    ),\r\n]\r\n\r\nEDUCATION = [\r\n    (\r\n        \"Ph.D., Computational Biology\",\r\n        \"Baywood Institute of Technology · 2014–2019\",\r\n        \"Dissertation: “Deep Learning Models for Decoding Neural Population Activity”\",\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"M.Sc., Bioinformatics\",\r\n        \"Riverbend University · 2012–2014\",\r\n        \"Thesis: “Statistical Methods for Single-Cell RNA-Seq Analysis”\",\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"B.Sc., Computer Science\",\r\n        \"Crestfield College of Engineering · 2008–2012\",\r\n        \"Graduated magna cum laude; President, Data Science Club\",\r\n    ),\r\n]\r\n\r\nPROJECTS = [\r\n    (\r\n        \"DeepVision: High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping\",\r\n        \"Lead Developer & Project Coordinator\",\r\n        [\r\n            \"Designed a PyTorch-based pipeline to segment two-photon images of mouse visual cortex.\",\r\n            \"Integrated temporal convolutional networks to predict stimulus orientation from calcium-imaging traces.\",\r\n            \"Deployed a Dockerized microservice for real-time data processing with Cascade Imaging Lab.\",\r\n        ],\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis\",\r\n        \"Principal Investigator\",\r\n        [\r\n            \"Constructed graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes from electron microscopy.\",\r\n            \"Trained GNNs to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.\",\r\n            \"Published an open-source toolkit in the NeuroTools suite, adopted by 12 labs worldwide.\",\r\n        ],\r\n    ),\r\n    (\r\n        \"CellMap: Multi-Modal Single-Cell Atlas\",\r\n        \"Co-Principal Investigator\",\r\n        [\r\n            \"Developed a Nextflow workflow combining scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data.\",\r\n            \"Implemented Bayesian clustering to resolve cell-type hierarchies in human cortical organoids.\",\r\n            \"Presented at the International Conference on Single-Cell Genomics (ICSCG) 2023.\",\r\n        ],\r\n    ),\r\n]\r\n\r\nTEACHING = [\r\n    (\"Undergraduate Course\", \"“Introduction to Computational Neuroscience” (Spring 2025)\"),\r\n    (\"Graduate Seminar\", \"“Advanced Machine Learning Methods in Biology” (Fall 2024)\"),\r\n    (\"Mentorship\", \"Supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master’s theses across neural data analysis and bioinformatics.\"),\r\n]\r\n\r\nSKILLS = [\r\n    (\"Languages\", \"Python, R, C++\"),\r\n    (\"Frameworks\", \"PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, NetworkX\"),\r\n    (\"Data Tools\", \"Nextflow, Snakemake, Docker, Kubernetes\"),\r\n    (\"Analysis\", \"MATLAB, Jupyter, Seurat, Scanpy\"),\r\n    (\"Visualization\", \"D3.js, Plotly, Matplotlib\"),\r\n]\r\n\r\nPUBLICATIONS = [\r\n    {\r\n        \"year\": \"2024\",\r\n        \"authors\": \"Moreno, L., & Patel, A.\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Temporal Convolutional Networks Decode Visual Stimuli from Two-Photon Signals\",\r\n        \"journal\": \"Journal of Computational Neuroscience\",\r\n        \"volume\": \"45(2)\",\r\n        \"pages\": \"123–137\",\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"year\": \"2023\",\r\n        \"authors\": \"Moreno, L., Zhang, W., & Singh, R.\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Graph Embedding Techniques Reveal Synaptic Motifs in EM Datasets\",\r\n        \"journal\": \"Neuroinformatics\",\r\n        \"volume\": \"21(4)\",\r\n        \"pages\": \"299–312\",\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"year\": \"2022\",\r\n        \"authors\": \"Moreno, L., et al.\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Integrative Single-Cell Atlas of Human Cerebral Organoids\",\r\n        \"journal\": \"Cell Systems\",\r\n        \"volume\": \"9(1)\",\r\n        \"pages\": \"67–82\",\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"year\": \"2021\",\r\n        \"authors\": \"Chen, J., Moreno, L., & Russo, M.\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Explainable AI Techniques in Neural Decoding\",\r\n        \"journal\": \"Frontiers in Neuroscience\",\r\n        \"volume\": \"15\",\r\n        \"pages\": \"756843\",\r\n    },\r\n]\r\n\r\nBLOG_POSTS = [\r\n    {\r\n        \"slug\": \"interpretable-deep-learning-neuroscience\",\r\n        \"date\": \"March 2025\",\r\n        \"date_iso\": \"2025-03-12\",\r\n        \"category\": \"Interpretability\",\r\n        \"read_time\": \"6 min read\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience\",\r\n        \"excerpt\": \"A model can predict the next neural response without telling us how the circuit works. Here is the design process I use to close that gap.\",\r\n        \"body\": [\r\n            (\"p\", \"A predictive model is not automatically a scientific explanation. In neuroscience, this distinction matters: a network can decode a stimulus \r\nfrom calcium-imaging traces while relying on artifacts, correlated features, or a shortcut that has little to do with the biological computation we hoped to \r\nstudy.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Begin with the scientific question\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Interpretability work should start before the architecture is chosen. I ask what claim the model is meant to support. Is it a decoder that \r\ncan support a brain–computer interface? A hypothesis about which neural populations carry information? Or a tool for discovering latent structure in a large \r\nrecording? Each goal imposes different validity requirements and suggests different explanations.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"For decoding studies, I favor models with explicit bottlenecks and well-defined inputs. Temporal convolutional networks are often a good \r\nbaseline because their receptive fields can be inspected and their latency structure can be compared with known physiology. For circuit-level questions, \r\ngraph-based representations are more natural when the biological object is relational.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Build a ladder of explanations\"),\r\n"]
[267.611013, "o", "            (\"p\", \"I use several complementary explanations rather than a single saliency map. First, global feature importance tells me whether the model is \r\nrelying on plausible channels or time windows. Second, local attributions reveal how a prediction changes around individual trials. Third, ablation tests \r\nestablish whether a claimed signal is necessary, not merely correlated. Finally, synthetic perturbations help identify failure modes that are invisible in a \r\nheld-out set.\"),\r\n            (\"blockquote\", \"An explanation should survive the same scrutiny we apply to any other scientific measurement.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Validate against the biology\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"The most useful checks are often simple. Does the model's preferred temporal window match the stimulus onset? Are attributions stable across \r\nanimals and sessions? Does performance collapse when a plausible nuisance variable is randomized? These tests connect the model back to the experimental design \r\nand make the resulting claims easier to falsify.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"None of this removes the need for careful experimental work. But it can turn a high-performing model into a sharper instrument for asking \r\nbiological questions—and a more honest account of what the data actually support.\"),\r\n        ],\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"slug\": \"machine-learning-single-cell-genomics\",\r\n        \"date\": \"January 2025\",\r\n        \"date_iso\": \"2025-01-21\",\r\n        \"category\": \"Single-Cell\",\r\n        \"read_time\": \"5 min read\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics\",\r\n        \"excerpt\": \"Both fields work with high-dimensional, noisy observations. The productive overlap is not a shared algorithm; it is a shared discipline of \r\nrepresentation and validation.\",\r\n        \"body\": [\r\n            (\"p\", \"Single-cell genomics and machine learning are often described as an obvious pairing: large matrices in, biological insight out. The reality \r\nis more interesting. Much of the value comes from deciding what a representation should preserve, how batch effects should be separated from biology, and which \r\nforms of validation are credible.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Representation is a scientific choice\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"A cell-by-gene matrix is already a representation. Normalization, feature selection, and embedding choices determine what downstream \r\nclustering can discover. I try to make those choices explicit and to compare pipelines across several reasonable alternatives. A result that exists only under \r\none normalization scheme is a fragile result, not a biological fact.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Multi-modal data sharpen the problem. scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial assays observe different layers of the same system. Integration \r\nmethods can align these layers, but alignment is not the same as explanation. I prefer to evaluate whether an integrated representation recovers known cell \r\ntypes, preserves condition-specific signals, and remains stable across donors.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Use ML where it changes the question\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Machine learning is most useful in this setting when it enables a question that would otherwise be impractical: latent-factor models for \r\ncontinuous cell states, graph methods for spatial neighborhoods, or Bayesian clustering for hierarchical cell-type structure. The point is not to add a neural \r\nnetwork to a familiar pipeline, but to make a previously inaccessible measurement tractable.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Validation should combine quantitative benchmarks with biological adjudication. Marker recovery, held-out donor performance, perturbation \r\nconsistency, and spatial coherence each test a different part of the claim. A model that is excellent on one axis can be misleading on another.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Keep the pipeline inspectable\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"The best computational biology is reproducible. I favor workflow systems such as Nextflow or Snakemake, explicit versioning, and outputs that\r\ncan be inspected at each stage. Interpretability here is practical: a collaborator should be able to trace how a biological conclusion emerged from a raw count \r\nmatrix.\"),\r\n        ],\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"slug\": \"graph-neural-networks-connectomics\",\r\n        \"date\": \"November 2024\",\r\n        \"date_iso\": \"2024-11-08\",\r\n        \"category\": \"Connectomics\",\r\n        \"read_time\": \"7 min read\",\r\n        \"title\": \"Scaling Graph Neural Networks for Connectomics\",\r\n        \"excerpt\": \"Connectomic datasets are large, sparse, and biologically structured. Graph learning can expose synaptic motifs—but only if the pipeline \r\nrespects the scale and uncertainty of the data.\",\r\n        \"body\": [\r\n            (\"p\", \"Connectomics asks us to reason about a network whose nodes and edges are only partially observed. Reconstructed neuron meshes carry \r\nsegmentation uncertainty, synapse calls can be ambiguous, and the resulting graphs can contain millions of edges. Graph neural networks are a natural fit, but \r\nscaling them is as much a data-engineering problem as a modeling problem.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Treat the graph as a measurement\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"The first design decision is what counts as a node and an edge. A node might be a cell body, a reconstructed segment, or an abstract \r\ncompartment; an edge might represent a synapse, a spatial contact, or an inferred connection. These choices change the learning problem. I prefer to preserve \r\nmultiple relational views when possible and to evaluate models against biologically meaningful motifs rather than only node-level labels.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Respect sparsity and uncertainty\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Dense matrix operations quickly become wasteful. Sparse message passing, neighbor sampling, and partitioned training make large connectomes \r\ntractable without discarding their structure. Equally important is uncertainty: an edge predicted with low confidence should not be treated like a verified \r\nsynapse. Calibration and selective prediction are useful here because they let a downstream analyst decide where human review should focus.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"I also evaluate graph models under controlled graph perturbations. If a model's classification of synapse types changes dramatically after \r\nsmall, biologically plausible edits, the model may be learning from reconstruction artifacts rather than circuit structure.\"),\r\n            (\"h2\", \"Look for motifs, then test them\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Graph embeddings can reveal candidate connectivity motifs, but candidate motifs are not conclusions. The next step is to compare them with \r\nnull models that preserve degree distribution, spatial locality, or cell-type composition. That comparison is what turns a visually interesting cluster into a \r\nquantitative claim about circuit organization.\"),\r\n            (\"p\", \"Scaling the method is necessary but not sufficient. The goal is an inspectable, uncertainty-aware pipeline whose outputs can guide \r\nexperiments—and whose failures are visible enough to learn from.\"),\r\n        ],\r\n    },\r\n]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef icon(paths: str) -> str:\r\n    return (\r\n        '<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" '\r\n        'stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" '\r\n        f'stroke-linejoin=\"round\">{paths}</svg>'\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef page(\r\n    *,\r\n    title: str,\r\n    description: str,\r\n    body: str,\r\n    active: str,\r\n    root: str = \"\",\r\n    canonical: str | None = None,\r\n) -> str:\r\n    nav_items = [\r\n        (\"index.html\", \"About Me\"),\r\n        (\"blog.html\", \"Blog\"),\r\n        (\"publications.html\", \"Publications\"),\r\n    ]\r\n    nav = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f'<li><a href=\"{root}{href}\"'\r\n        f'{\" aria-current=\\\"page\\\"\" if href == active else \"\"}>{label}</a></li>'\r\n        for href, label in nav_items\r\n    )\r\n    canonical_tag = f'\\n  <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"{escape(canonical)}\">' if canonical else \"\"\r\n    return f\"\"\"<!doctype html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head>\r\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\r\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"{escape(description)}\">\r\n  <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0d6b62\">\r\n  <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"{escape(title)}\">\r\n  <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"{escape(description)}\">\r\n  <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\r\n  <title>{escape(title)} | Lydia Moreno</title>{canonical_tag}\r\n  <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"{root}assets/favicon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"{root}assets/styles.css\">\r\n  <script src=\"{root}assets/main.js\" defer></script>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n  <a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\r\n  <header class=\"site-header\">\r\n    <div class=\"container header-inner\">\r\n      <a class=\"brand\" href=\"{root}index.html\" aria-label=\"Lydia Moreno — home\">\r\n        <span class=\"brand-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">LM</span>\r\n        <span class=\"brand-text\"><strong>Lydia Moreno</strong><span>Computational Neuroscience</span></span>\r\n      </a>\r\n      <button class=\"nav-toggle\" type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"site-nav\">Menu</button>\r\n      <nav class=\"site-nav\" id=\"site-nav\" aria-label=\"Primary navigation\">\r\n        <ul class=\"nav-list\">\r\n          {nav}\r\n        </ul>\r\n      </nav>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </header>\r\n  {body}\r\n  <footer class=\"site-footer\">\r\n    <div class=\"container footer-inner\">\r\n      <div>\r\n        <p class=\"footer-brand\">Lydia Moreno, PhD</p>\r\n        <p class=\"footer-note\">Computational neuroscience, interpretable machine learning, and single-cell data.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n      <ul class=\"footer-links\">\r\n        <li><a href=\"mailto:{EMAIL}\">Email</a></li>\r\n        <li><a href=\"{GITHUB}\" rel=\"me\">GitHub</a></li>\r\n        <li><a href=\"{TWITTER}\" rel=\"me\">Twitter</a></li>\r\n      </ul>\r\n      <p class=\"footer-meta\">© <span data-current-year>2026</span> Lydia Moreno. Research profile built as a static, accessible website.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </footer>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef about_body() -> str:\r\n    interests = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"\"\"<article class=\"interest-card\">\r\n          <div class=\"icon-badge\">{icon(svg)}</div>\r\n          <h3>{escape(title)}</h3>\r\n          <p>{escape(text)}</p>\r\n        </article>\"\"\"\r\n        for title, text, svg in RESEARCH_INTERESTS\r\n    )\r\n    education = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"\"\"<li>\r\n          <h3>{escape(degree)}</h3>\r\n          <p class=\"timeline-meta\">{escape(meta)}</p>\r\n          <p>{escape(detail)}</p>\r\n        </li>\"\"\"\r\n        for degree, meta, detail in EDUCATION\r\n    )\r\n    projects = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"\"\"<article class=\"project-card\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"project-role\">{escape(role)}</p>\r\n            <h3>{escape(title)}</h3>\r\n            <ul>{''.join(f'<li>{escape(point)}</li>' for point in points)}</ul>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"align-self:center; justify-self:end; color:var(--accent); opacity:.65;\">{icon('<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8\"/><path \r\nd=\"M12 8v8M8 12h8\"/>')}</div>\r\n        </article>\"\"\"\r\n        for title, role, points in PROJECTS\r\n    )\r\n    teaching = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"<li><strong>{escape(label)}</strong>{escape(text)}</li>\" for label, text in TEACHING\r\n    )\r\n    skills = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"<li><strong>{escape(label)}</strong>{escape(text)}</li>\" for label, text in SKILLS\r\n    )\r\n    return f\"\"\"\r\n  <main id=\"main\">\r\n    <section class=\"hero\">\r\n      <div class=\"container hero-grid\">\r\n        <div class=\"hero-copy\">\r\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">Research Profile</p>\r\n          <h1>Lydia Moreno, <span>PhD</span></h1>\r\n          <p class=\"hero-role\">Associate Professor of Computational Neuroscience</p>\r\n          <p class=\"hero-affiliation\">Riverbend University · School of Biological Sciences</p>\r\n          <p class=\"hero-lede\">I build interpretable machine learning methods that help reveal how neural circuits encode, process, and transform complex \r\nsensory information.</p>\r\n          <div class=\"hero-actions\">\r\n            <a class=\"button button-primary\" href=\"publications.html\">Explore publications {icon('<path d=\"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>')}</a>\r\n            <a class=\"button button-secondary\" href=\"mailto:{EMAIL}\">Get in touch</a>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <ul class=\"hero-facts\" aria-label=\"Profile highlights\">\r\n            <li><strong>15+</strong> peer-reviewed works</li>\r\n            <li><strong>20</strong> graduate researchers mentored</li>\r\n            <li><strong>3</strong> open research tools</li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <aside class=\"profile-card\" aria-label=\"Profile summary\">\r\n          <div class=\"monogram\" aria-hidden=\"true\">LM</div>\r\n          <p class=\"profile-kicker\">Research focus</p>\r\n          <h2>Neural computation, made interpretable.</h2>\r\n          <ul class=\"tag-list\" aria-label=\"Research areas\">\r\n            <li>Neural decoding</li>\r\n            <li>Biomedical imaging</li>\r\n            <li>Single-cell omics</li>\r\n            <li>Explainable AI</li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n          <ul class=\"contact-list\">\r\n            <li>{icon('<path d=\"M4 6h16v12H4z\"/><path d=\"m4 7 8 6 8-6\"/>')}<a href=\"mailto:{EMAIL}\">{EMAIL}</a></li>\r\n            <li>{icon('<path d=\"M12 21s7-5.3 7-12a7 7 0 1 0-14 0c0 6.7 7 12 7 12Z\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"9\" r=\"2.5\"/>')}<span>Blakely Hall, Room 312<br>Riverbend\r\nUniversity</span></li>\r\n            <li>{icon('<circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M8.5 9.5c.4-1 1.6-1.4 2.5-1.1 1.2.4 1.2 1.8.9 2.6-.3.9-1.5 1.4-1.5 2.4 0 .7.5 1.3 1.2 1.4M12 \r\n17.2v.1\"/>')} <a href=\"{TWITTER}\" rel=\"me\">@LydiaNeuroLab</a></li>\r\n            <li>{icon('<path d=\"M9 19c-4.3 1.3-4.3-2.1-6-2.5M15 21v-3.4c0-1 .1-1.4-.5-2 2.8-.3 5.5-1.3 5.5-6a4.7 4.7 0 0 0-1.3-3.3c.1-.4.6-1.6-.1-3.2 0 \r\n0-1-.3-3.3 1.2a11.2 11.2 0 0 0-6 0C7 2.8 6 3.1 6 3.1c-.7 1.6-.2 2.8-.1 3.2A4.7 4.7 0 0 0 4.5 9.6c0 4.7 2.7 5.7 5.5 6-.6.6-.6 1.2-.5 2V21\"/>')}<a href=\"{GITHUB}\"\r\nrel=\"me\">github.com/lydia-moreno</a></li>\r\n          </ul>\r\n        </aside>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section section-tight\" id=\"about\">\r\n      <div class=\"container two-col\">\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">About Me</p>\r\n          <h2>Questions first, then models.</h2>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"prose\">\r\n          <p>Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University’s School of Biological Sciences. Her work sits at \r\nthe intersection of machine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics, aiming to unravel how neural circuits encode and process complex sensory \r\ninformation.</p>\r\n          <p>She received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging\r\nanalysis at Northborough Research Center. Her research combines theory-driven modeling with open, reproducible computational pipelines.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section surface-band\" aria-labelledby=\"interests-heading\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"section-heading\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">Research Interests</p>\r\n            <h2 id=\"interests-heading\">Where the work lives</h2>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <p>Methods and questions that connect neural measurements to interpretable computational accounts.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"card-grid\">{interests}</div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section\" aria-labelledby=\"education-heading\">\r\n      <div class=\"container two-col\">\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">Education</p>\r\n          <h2 id=\"education-heading\">Training &amp; foundations</h2>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <ol class=\"timeline\">{education}</ol>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section surface-band\" aria-labelledby=\"projects-heading\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"section-heading\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">Selected Projects</p>\r\n            <h2 id=\"projects-heading\">Tools built for real data</h2>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <p>Open, collaborative projects spanning imaging, connectomics, and multi-modal cell atlases.</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"project-grid\">{projects}</div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section\" aria-labelledby=\"teaching-heading\">\r\n      <div class=\"container split-grid\">\r\n        <article class=\"teaching-card\">\r\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">Teaching &amp; Mentorship</p>\r\n          <h2 id=\"teaching-heading\" style=\"font-size:2rem;\">Building the next questions</h2>\r\n          <ul class=\"teaching-list\">{teaching}</ul>\r\n        </article>\r\n        <article class=\"skill-card\">\r\n          <p class=\"eyebrow\">Skills &amp; Tools</p>\r\n          <h2 style=\"font-size:2rem;\">A practical toolkit</h2>\r\n          <ul class=\"skill-list\">{skills}</ul>\r\n        </article>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"section section-tight\" aria-labelledby=\"contact-heading\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"contact-banner\">\r\n          <div>\r\n            <p class=\"eyebrow\">Collaboration</p>\r\n            <h2 id=\"contact-heading\">Let’s connect theory to data.</h2>\r\n            <p>I welcome conversations about interpretable machine learning, neural data science, and collaborative projects that need rigorous computational \r\nmethods.</p>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <a class=\"button\" href=\"mailto:{EMAIL}\">Email Lydia</a>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n  </main>\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef blog_body() -> str:\r\n    cards = \"\\n\".join(\r\n        f\"\"\"<article class=\"blog-card\">\r\n          <div class=\"blog-card-body\">\r\n            <p class=\"blog-date\">{escape(post['date'])} · {escape(post['category'])}</p>\r\n            <h3><a href=\"blog/{post['slug']}.html\">{escape(post['title'])}</a></h3>\r\n            <p class=\"blog-excerpt\">{escape(post['excerpt'])}</p>\r\n            <div class=\"blog-card-footer\">\r\n              <span>{escape(post['read_time'])}</span>\r\n              <a href=\"blog/{post['slug']}.html\" aria-label=\"Read {escape(post['title'])}\">Read note →</a>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </article>\"\"\"\r\n        for post in BLOG_POSTS\r\n    )\r\n    return f\"\"\"\r\n  <main id=\"main\">\r\n    <section class=\"page-hero\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Notes &amp; Ideas</p>\r\n        <h1>Blog</h1>\r\n        <p class=\"lede\">Occasional writing on neural computation, interpretable machine learning, and the craft of turning complex data into scientific \r\nclaims.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n    <section class=\"page-body\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"filter-bar\">\r\n          <div class=\"filter-group\" aria-label=\"Blog topics\">\r\n            <span class=\"filter-button\" aria-pressed=\"true\">All notes</span>\r\n            <span class=\"filter-button\">Interpretability</span>\r\n            <span class=\"filter-button\">Single-cell</span>\r\n            <span class=\"filter-button\">Connectomics</span>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"blog-grid\">{cards}</div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n  </main>\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef publications_body() -> str:\r\n    cards = []\r\n    for publication in PUBLICATIONS:\r\n        citation = (\r\n            f\"{publication['authors']} ({publication['year']}). \"\r\n            f\"“{publication['title']}.” {publication['journal']}, \"\r\n            f\"{publication['volume']}, {publication['pages']}.\"\r\n        )\r\n        cards.append(\r\n            f\"\"\"<article class=\"publication-card\" data-publication data-year=\"{publication['year']}\">\r\n              <div class=\"publication-year\">{publication['year']}</div>\r\n              <div>\r\n                <div class=\"publication-meta\"><span>Peer-reviewed article</span><span>{escape(publication['journal'])}</span></div>\r\n                <h2>{escape(publication['title'])}</h2>\r\n                <p class=\"publication-authors\">{escape(publication['authors'])}</p>\r\n                <p class=\"publication-venue\"><em>{escape(publication['journal'])}</em>, {escape(publication['volume'])}, {escape(publication['pages'])}.</p>\r\n                <div class=\"pub-footer\">\r\n                  <button class=\"copy-button\" type=\"button\" data-copy-citation=\"{escape(citation)}\">Copy citation</button>\r\n                  <span class=\"copy-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></span>\r\n                </div>\r\n              </div>\r\n            </article>\"\"\"\r\n        )\r\n    years = sorted({publication[\"year\"] for publication in PUBLICATIONS}, reverse=True)\r\n    filters = \"\".join(\r\n        f'<button class=\"filter-button\" type=\"button\" data-filter=\"{year}\" aria-pressed=\"false\">{year}</button>'\r\n        for year in years\r\n    )\r\n    return f\"\"\"\r\n  <main id=\"main\">\r\n    <section class=\"page-hero\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">Scholarship</p>\r\n        <h1>Publications</h1>\r\n        <p class=\"lede\">Peer-reviewed work on neural decoding, connectomics, single-cell genomics, and explainable AI. Filter by year or search titles, authors,\r\nand journals.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n    <section class=\"page-body\">\r\n      <div class=\"container\">\r\n        <div class=\"filter-bar\">\r\n          <div class=\"filter-group\" aria-label=\"Filter publications by year\">\r\n            <button class=\"filter-button\" type=\"button\" data-filter=\"all\" aria-pressed=\"true\">All</button>\r\n            {filters}\r\n          </div>\r\n          <label class=\"search-field\">Search publications\r\n            <input type=\"search\" data-publication-search placeholder=\"Title, author, or journal\">\r\n          </label>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"publication-list\" data-publication-list>\r\n          {''.join(cards)}\r\n        </div>\r\n        <p class=\"empty-state\" data-publication-empty hidden>No publications match that filter. Try a different year or search term.</p>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n  </main>\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef article_body(post: dict) -> str:\r\n    blocks = []\r\n    for kind, text in post[\"body\"]:\r\n        if kind == \"h2\":\r\n            blocks.append(f\"<h2>{escape(text)}</h2>\")\r\n        elif kind == \"blockquote\":\r\n            blocks.append(f\"<blockquote>{escape(text)}</blockquote>\")\r\n        else:\r\n            blocks.append(f\"<p>{escape(text)}</p>\")\r\n    return f\"\"\"\r\n  <main id=\"main\">\r\n    <article class=\"article-shell\">\r\n      <header class=\"article-header\">\r\n        <a class=\"back-link\" href=\"../blog.html\">← All notes</a>\r\n        <p class=\"eyebrow\">{escape(post['category'])}</p>\r\n        <h1>{escape(post['title'])}</h1>\r\n        <p class=\"article-meta\"><span>{escape(post['date'])}</span><span>{escape(post['read_time'])}</span><span>By Lydia Moreno</span></p>\r\n      </header>\r\n      <div class=\"article-body\">\r\n        {''.join(blocks)}\r\n      </div>\r\n    </article>\r\n  </main>\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[267.611183, "o", "def write_outputs() -> None:\r\n    pages = {\r\n        \"index.html\": page(\r\n            title=\"About Me\",\r\n            description=\"Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University, working at the intersection of \r\nmachine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics.\",\r\n            body=about_body(),\r\n            active=\"index.html\",\r\n        ),\r\n        \"about.html\": page(\r\n            title=\"About Me\",\r\n            description=\"Learn about Dr. Lydia Moreno's research, education, projects, teaching, and computational neuroscience toolkit.\",\r\n            body=about_body(),\r\n            active=\"index.html\",\r\n            canonical=\"index.html\",\r\n        ),\r\n        \"blog.html\": page(\r\n            title=\"Blog\",\r\n            description=\"Notes by Lydia Moreno on interpretable machine learning, neural computation, single-cell genomics, and connectomics.\",\r\n            body=blog_body(),\r\n            active=\"blog.html\",\r\n        ),\r\n        \"publications.html\": page(\r\n            title=\"Publications\",\r\n            description=\"Peer-reviewed publications by Dr. Lydia Moreno on neural decoding, connectomics, single-cell genomics, and explainable AI.\",\r\n            body=publications_body(),\r\n            active=\"publications.html\",\r\n        ),\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    for filename, content in pages.items():\r\n        (ROOT / filename).write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n\r\n    (ROOT / \"blog\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\r\n    for post in BLOG_POSTS:\r\n        content = page(\r\n            title=post[\"title\"],\r\n            description=post[\"excerpt\"],\r\n            body=article_body(post),\r\n            active=\"blog.html\",\r\n            root=\"../\",\r\n        )\r\n        (ROOT / \"blog\" / f\"{post['slug']}.html\").write_text(content, encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    write_outputs()\r\n    print(\"Generated index.html, about.html, blog.html, publications.html, and blog posts.\")\r\nPY\r\npython3 scripts/generate_site.py && find . -maxdepth 2 -type f -not -path './.git/*' -print | sort\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠼\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
