[351.096764, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe final markup check looks correct. I’ll initialize the repository on `main`, verify the staged diff for whitespace/secret issues, commit the site, and attach\r\na clearly labeled dummy GitHub remote so the final push commands are ready to customize.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/my_website && set -e\r\nif [ ! -d .git ]; then git init -b main; fi\r\ngit config user.name \"Lydia Moreno\"\r\ngit config user.email \"lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu\"\r\ngit add .\r\ngit diff --cached --check\r\ngit status --short\r\nprintf '\\n--- gh availability ---\\n'\r\ncommand -v gh || echo 'gh CLI not installed in this environment'\r\nprintf '\\n--- staged size ---\\n'\r\ngit diff --cached --stat\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[351.098237, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠧\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[351.110153, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[351.112725, "o", "<returncode>\r\n2\r\n<output>\r\nInitialized empty Git repository in /app/my_website/.git/\r\nabout.html:35: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\nblog.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\nblog/graph-neural-networks-connectomics.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\nblog/interpretable-deep-learning-neuroscience.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\nblog/machine-learning-single-cell-genomics.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\nindex.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\ninfo.md:1: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## About  \r\ninfo.md:4: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Education  \r\ninfo.md:5: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Ph.D., Computational Biology**  \r\ninfo.md:6: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Baywood Institute of Technology, 2014–2019  \r\ninfo.md:7: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  • Dissertation: “Deep Learning Models for Decoding Neural Population Activity”  \r\ninfo.md:8: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **M.Sc., Bioinformatics**  \r\ninfo.md:9: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Riverbend University, 2012–2014  \r\ninfo.md:10: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  • Thesis: “Statistical Methods for Single‐Cell RNA‐Seq Analysis”  \r\ninfo.md:11: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **B.Sc., Computer Science**  \r\ninfo.md:12: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Crestfield College of Engineering, 2008–2012  \r\ninfo.md:13: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  • Graduated magna cum laude; President, Data Science Club  \r\ninfo.md:15: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Research Interests  \r\ninfo.md:16: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Neural Encoding & Decoding**  \r\ninfo.md:17: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Developing interpretable models that translate spike‐train data into behavioral predictions.  \r\ninfo.md:18: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Machine Learning for Biomedical Imaging**  \r\ninfo.md:19: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to magnetic resonance and two‐photon microscopy data.  \r\ninfo.md:20: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Single‐Cell Omics**  \r\ninfo.md:21: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  Designing scalable pipelines for integrating multi‐modal single‐cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.  \r\ninfo.md:22: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Explainable AI in Neuroscience**  \r\ninfo.md:25: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Selected Projects  \r\ninfo.md:26: trailing whitespace.\r\n+### 1. DeepVision: High‐Resolution Neural Activity Mapping  \r\ninfo.md:27: trailing whitespace.\r\n+**Role**: Lead Developer & Project Coordinator  \r\ninfo.md:28: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Designed a PyTorch‐based pipeline to segment two‐photon images of mouse visual cortex.  \r\ninfo.md:29: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Integrated temporal convolutional networks to predict stimulus orientation from calcium‐imaging traces.  \r\ninfo.md:32: trailing whitespace.\r\n+### 2. NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis  \r\ninfo.md:33: trailing whitespace.\r\n+**Role**: Principal Investigator  \r\ninfo.md:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Constructed graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes from electron‐microscopy.  \r\ninfo.md:35: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Trained GNNs to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.  \r\ninfo.md:38: trailing whitespace.\r\n+### 3. CellMap: Multi‐Modal Single‐Cell Atlas  \r\ninfo.md:39: trailing whitespace.\r\n+**Role**: Co‐Principal Investigator  \r\ninfo.md:40: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Developed a Nextflow workflow combining scRNA‐Seq, ATAC‐Seq, and spatial FISH data.  \r\ninfo.md:41: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- Implemented Bayesian clustering to resolve cell‐type hierarchies in human cortical organoids.  \r\ninfo.md:44: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Publications  \r\ninfo.md:45: trailing whitespace.\r\n+1. Moreno, L., & Patel, A. (2024). “Temporal Convolutional Networks Decode Visual Stimuli from Two‐Photon Signals.” *Journal of Computational Neuroscience*, \r\n45(2), 123–137.  \r\ninfo.md:46: trailing whitespace.\r\n+2. Moreno, L., Zhang, W., & Singh, R. (2023). “Graph Embedding Techniques Reveal Synaptic Motifs in EM Datasets.” *Neuroinformatics*, 21(4), 299–312.  \r\ninfo.md:47: trailing whitespace.\r\n+3. Moreno, L. et al. (2022). “Integrative Single‐Cell Atlas of Human Cerebral Organoids.” *Cell Systems*, "]
[351.112797, "o", "9(1), 67–82.  \r\ninfo.md:48: trailing whitespace.\r\n+4. Chen, J., Moreno, L., & Russo, M. (2021). “Explainable AI Techniques in Neural Decoding.” *Frontiers in Neuroscience*, 15, 756843.  \r\ninfo.md:50: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Blog  \r\ninfo.md:52: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **March 2025**: [Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience](#)  \r\ninfo.md:53: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **January 2025**: [Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics](#)  \r\ninfo.md:56: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Teaching & Mentorship  \r\ninfo.md:57: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Undergraduate Course**: “Introduction to Computational Neuroscience” (Spring 2025)  \r\ninfo.md:58: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Graduate Seminar**: “Advanced Machine Learning Methods in Biology” (Fall 2024)  \r\ninfo.md:59: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Mentorship**: Supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master’s theses on topics ranging from neural data analysis to bioinformatics pipelines.  \r\ninfo.md:61: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Skills & Tools  \r\ninfo.md:62: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Languages**: Python, R, C++  \r\ninfo.md:63: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Frameworks**: PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit‐learn, NetworkX  \r\ninfo.md:64: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Data Tools**: Nextflow, Snakemake, Docker, Kubernetes  \r\ninfo.md:65: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Analysis**: MATLAB, Jupyter, Seurat, Scanpy  \r\ninfo.md:66: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Visualization**: D3.js, Plotly, Matplotlib  \r\ninfo.md:68: trailing whitespace.\r\n+## Contact  \r\ninfo.md:69: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Email**: lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu  \r\ninfo.md:70: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Office**: Blakely Hall, Room 312, Riverbend University  \r\ninfo.md:71: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **Twitter**: [@LydiaNeuroLab](https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab)  \r\ninfo.md:72: trailing whitespace.\r\n+- **GitHub**: [github.com/lydia‐moreno](https://github.com/lydia‐moreno)  \r\npublications.html:34: trailing whitespace.\r\n+  \r\n\r\n"]
